      "side": 1,
      "message": "The patch looks good to me. Here\u0027s why the reference has no actual issue:\n\nIn the reference, `ref8 - offset` (fake byte pointer and adjusted by offset bytes) is passed directly to `aom_highbd_convolve8_horiz()`.\n\nIn this CL, `ref8` is first converted to a short pointer: `ref \u003d ref8 \u003c\u003c 1`. Since `ref` is a short pointer, `ref - offset` adjusts the address by 2 bytes per offset:\n```\n\u003d (ref8 \u003c\u003c 1) - (offset \u003c\u003c 1)\n```\nThis is then converted back to a byte pointer via `CONVERT_TO_BYTEPTR`:\n```\n\u003d ((ref8 \u003c\u003c 1) - (offset \u003c\u003c 1)) \u003e\u003e 1\n\u003d ref8 - offset  (same as the reference)\n```\nSo the final address passed into `aom_highbd_convolve8_horiz()` is identical in both the reference and this CL.",
